|> Exercise
    handle=_lorentz_factor_dimensionality_

    If $v$ is a speed and $c$ is the speed of light, what
    is the dimension of the expression below?
    $$
    {1\over \sqrt{1 - {v^2\over c^2}}}
    $$
    (Known as the _Lorentz factor_.)
    !! ...?

    |> Solution

        Since

        $$
        {v \over c}
        $$
        
        is “speed over speed”, it is dimensionless,
        and since the sums, differences, squares,
        square roots, and reciprocals of dimensionless
        quantities are dimensionless, the entire
        expression is dimensionless.

        !! (Also dimensionless: “1 over dimensionless”
        !! is dimensionless.)
        !! (Because the reciprocal of a dimensionless
        !! quantity is dimensionless, the Lorentz factor
        !! is also dimensionless.)

        !! ...known as the _Lorentz factor_ in physics.
        !! presuming $c$ is the speed of light.
        !! Because the reciprocal of a dimensionless
        !! quantity is dimensionless, the Lorentz factor
        !! is just as dimensionless as its reciprocal,
        !! i.e., the square root that we studied.

        !! |> SolutionNote

        !!     Because the reciprocal of a dimensionless
        !!     quantity is dimensionless, the Lorentz factor
        !!     is also dimensionless. (In case you had any nagging
        !!     doubts.)
